- **hammerspoon**: Hammerspoon is the one signed app holding Accessibility and Screen Recording, so agent tools that read the screen or drive the mouse and keyboard run inside it, and permissions are granted once. Config: `~/.hammerspoon/init.lua` (linked from the harness); project extensions go in `~/.hammerspoon/local/*.lua`. Call it with `hs -c 'return harness.status()'` (screen locked? permissions on?). **Any task that needs the screen** (drives or reads an app's window, takes screenshots, clicks or types) runs under awake mode so the idle lock cannot stop it: wrap it as `awake run <name> -- <command>` (no idle lock, screen dimmed, locks when a person touches the Mac and when the command ends or dies). This applies to agents, firstmate crews and scripts alike; hcron jobs with `--needs gui` get it by themselves. Tools must tag their posted events with `harness.EVENT_TAG`. If the screen is already locked, stop and report it instead of retrying. Never build separate binaries that need their own permission grants. Status: `__HARNESS_DIR__/modules/hammerspoon/install.sh --status`.
